---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/indas/indas27.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Applicability" },
        { id: "s3", label: "When Separate Financial Statements Are Prepared" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Measurement Options – Cost, Ind AS 109, or Equity Method" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Dividends from Investees" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Group Reorganisations" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Mandatory Standalone Filing – The Indian Regulatory Divergence" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure of Investments" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Ind AS 27 vs IAS 27 – Full Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ============ SECTION 1 – CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK LINK ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Same measurement choice as IAS 27, mandatory Indian filing overlay</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 27 shares IAS 27's core content – when an entity PREPARES separate financial statements, investments in subsidiaries, joint ventures, and associates are accounted for EITHER at COST, in accordance with Ind AS 109 (fair value), or using the EQUITY METHOD. Where Ind AS 27 genuinely diverges in PRACTICE is that the Companies Act, 2013 makes standalone financial statement preparation MANDATORY for every Indian company, a legal requirement IAS 27 itself does not impose (since IFRS defers to LOCAL jurisdictional law on whether separate FS are required at all).</div>
        <div class="elabel">HOW IND AS 27 MAPS TO THE FRAMEWORK</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span><strong>Accountability</strong> – mandatory standalone reporting ensures EVERY Indian company (not just consolidating parents) provides a discrete, entity-level financial picture – a company-law-driven choice, not an Ind AS 27 accounting principle</span>
          <span><strong>Comparability</strong> – the measurement OPTIONS themselves (cost/Ind AS 109/equity method) are IDENTICAL to IAS 27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This mandatory filing requirement is a COMPANY LAW divergence, not a divergence in Ind AS 27's own accounting content – Ind AS 27's substantive MEASUREMENT rules are IDENTICAL to IAS 27.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Three measurement options – identical to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-16"><span>Option</span><span>Basis</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-16"><span>Cost</span><span>Historical cost less impairment</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-16"><span>Ind AS 109</span><span>Fair value through P&amp;L or OCI</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-16"><span>Equity method</span><span>Per Ind AS 28's mechanics</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 2 – SCOPE & DEFINITIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What Ind AS 27 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 27 prescribes accounting/disclosure for investments in subsidiaries, joint ventures, and associates WHEN an entity elects, or is required, to prepare separate financial statements – IDENTICAL scope to IAS 27.</div>
        <div class="note">In India, EVERY company must apply this standard, since standalone FS preparation is compulsory under the Companies Act, 2013.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions you must know</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Separate financial statements</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">IDENTICAL definition to IAS 27 – statements presented by a parent (or investor) in which investments are accounted for at cost, per Ind AS 109, or using the equity method, rather than on the basis of reported results and net assets of investees.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Standalone financial statements</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The Companies Act, 2013 terminology for an Indian company's separate financial statements, MANDATORY regardless of consolidation status.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 3 – WHEN PREPARED ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>When Separate Financial Statements Are Prepared</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Optional under IAS 27, mandatory under Indian company law</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">IAS 27 itself is NEUTRAL on whether separate financial statements must be prepared at all – this is left to jurisdictional law/regulation. Ind AS 27 (via Indian company law) makes them MANDATORY for every Indian company, in ADDITION to consolidated financial statements where applicable (see Section 7).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 4 – MEASUREMENT OPTIONS (worked example) ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Measurement Options – Cost, Ind AS 109, or Equity Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Identical choice to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example 1: Choosing a measurement basis for a subsidiary investment</div>
          <div class="wk-body">An Indian parent company holds a 100% investment in a subsidiary, originally acquired for ₹50 crore, with the subsidiary's fair value now estimated at ₹80 crore.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The parent may elect to carry this investment in its STANDALONE financial statements at COST (₹50 crore less any impairment), at FAIR VALUE under Ind AS 109 (₹80 crore, with changes through P&amp;L or OCI depending on the election), or using the EQUITY METHOD – an IDENTICAL choice to what IAS 27 offers globally, with the SAME accounting consequences for each option.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 5 – DIVIDENDS FROM INVESTEES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Dividends from Investees</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Identical to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Dividends from a subsidiary, JV, or associate are recognised in P&amp;L when the right to receive payment is established, with an assessment of whether the dividend indicates POSSIBLE impairment of the investment – IDENTICAL to IAS 27.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 6 – GROUP REORGANISATIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Group Reorganisations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Specific guidance for group reorganisations meeting defined criteria (e.g. establishing a new parent) applies IDENTICALLY to IAS 27, allowing the new parent to measure cost at the PREVIOUS carrying amount of its share of equity in the original parent.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 7 – MANDATORY STANDALONE FILING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Mandatory Standalone Filing – The Indian Regulatory Divergence</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">The single most important Ind AS 27-related Indian practical point</div>
        <div class="principle">Under the Companies Act, 2013, EVERY Indian company – even a wholly-owned subsidiary within a large group, or a parent that ALSO prepares consolidated financial statements – MUST prepare, have audited, and FILE its own STANDALONE financial statements with the Registrar of Companies (RoC), applying Ind AS 27's measurement options at the ENTITY level. This is a distinctly Indian statutory REQUIREMENT – many IFRS jurisdictions do NOT mandate separate financial statements for every entity in a group, particularly where only consolidated reporting is legally required.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 8 – DISCLOSURE OF INVESTMENTS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure of Investments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Identical to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Disclosure of the fact separate financial statements have been prepared, a list of significant investments, and the method used to account for them – IDENTICAL to IAS 27.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 9 – DISCLOSURE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Identical disclosure requirements to IAS 27</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Fact that the statements are separate, and reason for their preparation if not otherwise required</span>
          <span>List of significant investments and measurement basis used</span>
          <span>Name and registered office of the entity whose consolidated FS comply with Ind AS/IFRS</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 10 – JUDGMENTS & ESTIMATES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where management judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Selecting a CONSISTENT measurement policy across categories of investments</span>
              <span>Assessing indicators of impairment on investments carried at cost</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Fair value of investments measured under Ind AS 109</span>
              <span>Recoverable amount for impairment testing of cost-carried investments</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout warn callout--chip callout--warn-flush">Indian companies must maintain BOTH standalone and (where applicable) consolidated financial statements on an ONGOING basis, given the mandatory dual filing requirement – a genuinely significant compliance workload distinguishing Indian practice from some other IFRS jurisdictions.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 11 – IND AS 27 vs IAS 27 ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Ind AS 27 vs IAS 27 – Full Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comprehensive comparison table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>IAS 27</span><span>Ind AS 27</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-1-1"><span>Measurement options (cost/fair value/equity method)</span><span>Standard choice</span><span>IDENTICAL – no substantive divergence</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-1-1"><span>Requirement to prepare separate FS at all</span><span>Left to jurisdictional law – NOT mandated by IAS 27 itself</span><span>Companies Act, 2013 MANDATES standalone FS for every Indian company, regardless of consolidation status</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Ind AS 27's own MEASUREMENT content is essentially IDENTICAL to IAS 27 – the mandatory standalone filing requirement is a genuinely significant Indian COMPANY LAW divergence, not an accounting divergence within the standard itself.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 12 – STATEMENT MAPPING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Comprehensive event-to-statement mapping table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event / transaction</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Investment measured at cost/fair value</span><span><span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>In the standalone/separate financial statements</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Dividend received from investee</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised when the right to receive is established</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 13 – RELATED STANDARDS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>IAS 27</span><span>The global counterpart standard, converged in content with a mandatory Indian filing overlay</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>Companies Act, 2013</span><span>Mandates standalone financial statement preparation for every Indian company</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>Ind AS 110</span><span>Governs CONSOLIDATED financial statements, prepared alongside separate FS where applicable</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Registrar of Companies (RoC)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The Indian authority with which every company must file its standalone (and consolidated, where applicable) financial statements.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Group reorganisation</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A restructuring meeting defined criteria permitting carrying-amount-based cost measurement for a new parent – identical to IAS 27.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 14 – GLOSSARY ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Registrar of Companies (RoC)", definition: "The Indian authority with which every company must file its standalone (and consolidated, where applicable) financial statements." },
      { term: "Group reorganisation", definition: "A restructuring meeting defined criteria permitting carrying-amount-based cost measurement for a new parent – identical to IAS 27." },
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
